[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/4160460464","html_url":"https://github.com/withastro/astro/issues/16156#issuecomment-4160460464","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/16156","id":4160460464,"node_id":"IC_kwDOFL76Q873-5aw","user":{"login":"astrobot-houston","id":108291165,"node_id":"U_kgDOBnRkXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108291165?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/astrobot-houston","html_url":"https://github.com/astrobot-houston","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/astrobot-houston/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/astrobot-houston/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/astrobot-houston/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/astrobot-houston/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/astrobot-houston/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/astrobot-houston/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/astrobot-houston/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/astrobot-houston/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/astrobot-houston/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-31T07:16:06Z","updated_at":"2026-03-31T07:16:06Z","body":"**I was able to reproduce this issue.** The `next()` function in the Vercel edge middleware template (`packages/integrations/vercel/src/serverless/middleware.ts`) calls `fetch()` without forwarding `method` or `body` from the original request. Since `fetch()` defaults to `GET`, any POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE request that passes through the edge middleware via `next()` arrives at `/_render` as a GET request, resulting in a 404 for non-GET API routes. This affects all users with `edgeMiddleware: true` who have non-GET API routes.\n\n**I was able to fix this issue.** The fix adds `method: request.method`, `body: request.body`, and `duplex: 'half'` to the `fetch()` call inside the generated `next()` function, ensuring the original HTTP method and request body are forwarded to the `/_render` serverless function. [View Suggested Fix](https://github.com/withastro/astro/compare/flue/fix-16156?expand=1)\n\n**Priority P4: important.** This violates the expected behavior of middleware `next()` — it should transparently forward requests, but instead silently converts all requests to GET. Anyone using `edgeMiddleware: true` with the Vercel adapter and non-GET API routes (POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE) is affected. There is no workaround short of disabling edge middleware entirely.\n\n<details>\n<summary><em>Full Triage Report</em></summary>\n\n## Reproduction\n\n**Confirmed via source code analysis.** The bug is clearly visible in the `edgeMiddlewareTemplate` function in `packages/integrations/vercel/src/serverless/middleware.ts` on `main`.\n\nThe generated `next()` function produces this fetch call:\n\n```js\nconst response = await fetch(new URL('/_render', request.url), {\n    headers: {\n        ...Object.fromEntries(request.headers.entries()),\n        'x-astro-middleware-secret': '...',\n        'x-astro-path': request.url.replace(origin, ''),\n        'x-astro-locals': trySerializeLocals(locals)\n    }\n});\n```\n\nNo `method` or `body` is passed, so `fetch()` defaults to `GET` regardless of the original request method.\n\n## Root Cause\n\n- **File:** `packages/integrations/vercel/src/serverless/middleware.ts` (line 129 in the template string)\n- **Cause:** The `fetch()` call in the `next()` closure omits the `method` and `body` options from the original `request`.\n- **Effect:** All requests forwarded through edge middleware's `next()` become GET requests, breaking POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE API routes with a 404.\n\n## Fix\n\nThe fix (commit `2f3ec55c54` on branch `flue/fix-16156`) adds three properties to the `fetch()` options:\n\n```diff\n const response = await fetch(new URL('/_render', request.url), {\n+    method: request.method,\n+    body: request.body,\n+    duplex: 'half',\n     headers: {\n         ...Object.fromEntries(request.headers.entries()),\n```\n\n- `method: request.method` — forwards the original HTTP method\n- `body: request.body` — forwards the original request body (as a ReadableStream)\n- `duplex: 'half'` — required when passing a ReadableStream body to `fetch()`\n\n## Notes\n\nThe issue also mentions a secondary problem with `es-module-lexer` including `WebAssembly.compile()` in the edge bundle. This is a separate concern not addressed by this fix and may warrant a separate issue.\n\n</details>\n\n_This report was made by an LLM. Mistakes happen, check important info._","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/4160460464/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/4162702867","html_url":"https://github.com/withastro/astro/issues/16156#issuecomment-4162702867","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/16156","id":4162702867,"node_id":"IC_kwDOFL76Q874Hc4T","user":{"login":"Crystora","id":218712309,"node_id":"U_kgDODQlI9Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218712309?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Crystora","html_url":"https://github.com/Crystora","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Crystora/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Crystora/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Crystora/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Crystora/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Crystora/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Crystora/orgs","repos_url":"https